WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.670
(Leaves rustling)

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.504
(Light clicks on)

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:06.298
Ow!

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.174
Jimmy:
Release me!

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:09.343
Hello.

00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:10.344
You're in my bushes.

00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:11.386
Jimmy:
They’re really well-kept.

00:00:11.762 --> 00:00:12.429
(Exhales)

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:13.472
How's Alice doing?

00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:14.723
Liz:
You okay Alice?

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:16.725
Liz:
I have to ask, 

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.269
is this you forever?

00:00:19.895 --> 00:00:20.687
I don't know.

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:24.399
♪♪

00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:26.902
Bill Lawrence:
I always had in the back of my
head 

00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:29.696
writing a show about a-a
physician or a

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.990
Bill Lawrence:
therapist that was kind of
dealing with grief.

00:00:32.324 --> 00:00:33.617
Excuse me. Sup, Jimmy?

00:00:33.951 --> 00:00:34.868
Hey Gabby.

00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:38.247
Brett Goldstein:
And I had an idea for a show
that was basically

00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:41.500
a very, very dark version of
what this show is.

00:00:41.959 --> 00:00:43.085
Who are these girls, Jimmy?

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.461
Are they hookers?

00:00:44.503 --> 00:00:45.587
I don’t think so.

00:00:45.796 --> 00:00:46.797
Did you pay them money?

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:48.090
Not yet.

00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:51.885
And he said, why don’t we put
these together?

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.595
♪♪

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:56.223
Brett Goldstein:
We met with Jason, and we talked
about this idea for the show.

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:58.684
And then I thought very soon
after, he said, ‘Yeah, I want to

00:00:58.684 --> 00:00:59.601
Brett Goldstein:
do this with you guys.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.272
You meet Jimmy truly at
rock-bottom.

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.315
Jason Segel:
He's grieving the loss of his
wife.

00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:08.402
♪♪

00:01:08.402 --> 00:01:11.655
You’ve been acting like it only
happened to you, but it happened
to us.

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:14.992
Jason Segel:
Jimmy has really fallen apart
and is no longer a dependable parent.

00:01:15.284 --> 00:01:17.577
You know who the most important
person in your life is?

00:01:17.953 --> 00:01:18.495
You.

00:01:18.662 --> 00:01:19.788
Your daughter.

00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:20.998
Right, that’s what I meant.

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.124
I'm second.

00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:23.333
Okay.

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:27.129
♪It's a new day tomorrow♪

00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:29.965
Because of his grieving, things
reach a boiling point.

00:01:30.173 --> 00:01:32.301
Jimmy:
You guys ever get so mad at your
patients?

00:01:32.301 --> 00:01:34.303
(Mocking voice)
I get sad when I do this thing.

00:01:34.303 --> 00:01:34.720
Haha.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.679
-Maybe don’t do that thing!

00:01:36.138 --> 00:01:39.266
Jimmy decides to start telling
patients exactly what he thinks.

00:01:40.142 --> 00:01:41.143
What sets you off?

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:41.977
Everything.

00:01:41.977 --> 00:01:42.853
You trust me, Sean?

00:01:42.853 --> 00:01:43.228
-No.

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:43.728
Jimmy:
Doesn’t matter.

00:01:44.146 --> 00:01:45.605
Let’s go find you someone to
beat up.

00:01:45.731 --> 00:01:47.816
♪Take a breath and believe♪

00:01:49.568 --> 00:01:50.777
Oh, he can use his feet.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.029
Sean, he’s using his feet!

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:53.864
He’s gonna use his feet the
whole time, I bet.

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:54.531
I know that.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.201
♪There's a wide, wide world in
front of you♪

00:01:58.201 --> 00:02:00.412
If you don’t feel any grief or
heartbreak,

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:03.498
Jessica Williams:
then you’ve missed the point of
what it means to be alive.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:06.209
Sometimes you’re crying, and
it’s very surprising,

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:07.502
but it’s very funny.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.253
Aha!

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:09.087
(Crash)

00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:10.255
Ahh!

00:02:10.464 --> 00:02:11.340
I’m so sorry.

00:02:11.757 --> 00:02:13.175
How are you already crying so
hard?

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.676
Oh, no, 

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:16.303
I was crying before.

00:02:16.428 --> 00:02:20.015
♪♪

00:02:20.015 --> 00:02:23.185
Jason Segel:
Throughout the season, we watch
Jimmy clumsily

00:02:23.185 --> 00:02:25.020
figure out how to rebuild.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.063
Dr. Phil Rhodes:
Be me for a second.

00:02:26.188 --> 00:02:28.106
Sorry for always being so hard
on you.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:29.816
It’s only ‘cause I love ya.

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:31.276
I don’t talk like that.

00:02:31.777 --> 00:02:32.611
(Crying)

00:02:32.611 --> 00:02:34.529
Brett Goldstein:
It’s the journey of reconnecting
with

00:02:34.529 --> 00:02:35.989
all the people that surround
him.

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:37.324
I was there!

00:02:37.324 --> 00:02:38.784
I needed to hit rock-bottom,

00:02:38.784 --> 00:02:39.493
Jimmy:
and you wouldn’t let me.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.328
Jason Segel:
A really interesting theme of
the show

00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:42.871
is by helping others,

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:44.831
we can somehow heal ourselves.

00:02:45.082 --> 00:02:46.458
Bill Lawrence:
When there’s a big cloud of
darkness,

00:02:46.458 --> 00:02:48.126
sometimes the only thing that
can yank you out

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:49.503
Bill Lawrence:
is making each other laugh.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.463
Man, this thing I’m doing is
really working.

00:02:51.505 --> 00:02:53.423
♪♪

00:02:54.091 --> 00:02:55.384
I need you to be excited for me.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:59.262
♪It's a new day tomorrow♪

00:02:59.429 --> 00:03:00.055
I love you.

00:03:00.097 --> 00:03:03.141
♪♪

00:03:03.141 --> 00:03:03.600
Too much.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.810
Yes, I know.

